Never quit.  Never never never never.  (Well, maybe if one of the
items required to finish the game is permanently lost - but then
only if you're completely sure it's completely gone.  Never quit 
because you're low on hit points).

There are lots of things which could have saved you with only 1 hit 
point left surrouded by nasties:

1) teleportation - lots of ways to teleport: read a scroll, zap
   yourself with a wand, teleport spell, read a tough spellbook and 
   get wrenched, ^T if you're at a high enough level.  If you have any 
   unidentified scrolls/wands or any spellbooks, you've got a chance.  
   If you manage to teleport, try to either get to the stairs, or
   get to a dead-end hall where you can fight the monsters one at
   a time (preferably at a distance by zapping your best wand).

2) Digging: zap a wand/spell of digging at the floor.

3) Polymorph - zapping an un-identified wand at yourself may teleport
   you, or might turn you into a Vampire Lord with 70 HP.  You never
   know.

4) The good old engrave Elbereth trick (although it might not work
   on all monsters).  Try a wand of fire if you've got one.

5) A scare monster scroll.  Read it or drop it.  Another good reason
   to try reading an unidentified scroll.

6) magic flute: Puts monster to sleep.

7) magic harp: tames monstes

8) Amulet of life saving - maybe you have an unidetified amulet
   that you didn't put on because it was cursed.  You never can tell.

9) Run away, Run away: If you're not completely surrounded, give it a 
   try.  This will save you if you're faster than the monsters.

10) Hack and slash: Even if you only have one hit point, the monsters
    might miss.  Attack the biggest monster with your nastiest attack,
    and hope you kill him and that the others miss.  (It can't be any
    worse than quitting)

I really wouldn't worry about leaving a bones file.  By the time most 
people get to level 12, they should be able to take on just about any
bones level.  I normally hope to run into them, just for the chance of
getting loot.  The only really nasty bones levels are the ones early 
on with polymorph traps. If you put on a blindfold whenever you get to 
a level, you'll know if the monsters are too tough for you, and avoid 
them (perhaps by digging down to the next level).
